{"format":1,"seq":82,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm planning to write a script that filters npm audit output against an ignore list, exposing a `filterAudit` function plus a CLI entry point, and I need to figure out where its test file should live alongside the existing test structure.\n\nThe algorithm iteratively prunes `via` entries from each vulnerability that match ignored advisories or reference packages no longer present, repeating until stable, then treats any remaining vulnerabilities as failures that should print a summary and exit nonzero. I'll run `npm audit --omit=dev --json` via spawnSync, parse its output, and handle cases where it exits nonzero or returns unparseable JSON.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01SK5yZzYy8kqtaaJhBKPrpE","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Check vitest config include patterns and test/support contents\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { glob, list } }) => {\n  const [c, s] = await Promise.all([glob([\"vitest.config.*\", \"tsconfig*.json\", \"oxlint*\", \".oxlintrc*\"]), list(\"test/support\")]);\n  return { c: c.entries, s: s as unknown as PitJsonValue };\n}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_017BfFAhwqdwhtdfLA3UBfWh","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read vitest config and tsconfig\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { batch } }) => {\n  const r = await batch([{ kind: \"read\", file: \"vitest.config.ts\", options: { format: \"raw\" } }, { kind: \"read\", file: \"tsconfig.json\", options: { format: \"raw\" } }]);\n  return r as unknown as PitJsonValue;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":840,"cacheRead":28280,"cacheWrite":4674,"totalTokens":33796,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":477},"stopReason